    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d638">

                <pb facs="0693" n="685" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg685"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.981/70: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-10-09T12:00:00+01:00">October 9,
                        1939—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received October 9—10:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1634. Department’s 605 [<hi rendition="#italic">665</hi>], October 7, 4
                        p.m.<anchor n="26" xml:id="d638-f1"/> As German authorities may shortly
                    complete arrangements for return to Warsaw of foreign representatives formerly
                    established there I recommend that Haering and Birkeland<anchor n="27"
                        xml:id="d638-f2"/> be authorized to proceed there as soon as such
                    arrangements have been made. It has been so far impossible for the Embassy to
                    communicate directly with Chylanski and the presence of Haering and Birkeland in
                    Warsaw should facilitate that matter as well as expedite the protection of
                    American property and assistance to American citizens in Warsaw. Reply
                        urgent<anchor n="28" xml:id="d638-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d638-f1" n="26" xml:id="d638-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d638-f2" n="27" xml:id="d638-f2-content">
                <p>Carl Birkeland, American Vice Consul at Warsaw.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d638-f3" n="28" xml:id="d638-f3-content">
                <p>Department’s telegram No. 695, October 11, 7 p.m., to the Ambassador in Germany,
                    stated that Haering and Birkeland Should proceed to Warsaw.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
